","summary":"Added `ProblemCode.SUSPICIOUS_TIMESTAMP` (declared last) plus a `Problem.suspiciousTimestamp(inputIndex, requestId, requestedAt)` factory, and made `WorkRequestValidator` clock-aware: a new `WorkRequestValidator(Clock)` overload (null-checked with message "clock") alongside the existing no-arg constructor defaulting to `Clock.systemUTC()`, reading `clock.instant()` once per `validate` call and appending a SUSPICIOUS_TIMESTAMP problem (after the field-order problems) for any parsed `requestedAt` strictly after that instant, with the trace note reason "future requestedAt". `ProcessingConfig` now exposes a `clock` bean returning `Clock.systemUTC()` and builds `workRequestValidator` with it; the generated order-independence batch gained one far-future request (size 200 → 201) so every ProblemCode stays covered.","uncertainties":["The generated batch's future request uses a hard-coded 2099 instant and id FUT-000/FEQ-0; if a test pins a specific id or count beyond hasSize(201) it may need adjusting.","BatchObserver needed no change since it already iterates ProblemCode.values(), so the new code automatically gets a counter.","Assumed the rejection-note reason wording for the new code is "future requestedAt" derived from the problem's field, as stated in the criteria."]}

